 ## Ways Claude can talk to Codex
 
+### 0. Where `codex` is, and which clients can actually run it
+
+Absolute path on this machine:
+
+```
+/Users/kjetil/.local/bin/codex
+```
+
+It is not reliably on `PATH`. Always invoke it by absolute path.
+
+That path is a symlink into the ChatGPT desktop app:
+
+```
+/Users/kjetil/.local/bin/codex -> /Applications/ChatGPT.app/Contents/Resources/codex
+```
+
+So Codex is not a standalone install. It ships inside ChatGPT.app, which means
+a ChatGPT app update or reinstall can move, replace or break the symlink, and
+removing the app removes Codex. If the symlink is dead, relink it rather than
+concluding that Codex is gone. The `codex-local` MCP server runs from the same
+binary.
+
+Reachability differs per client. This is the part that keeps getting lost and
+costing a round trip, so it is written down:
+
+| Surface | Can execute `/Users/kjetil/.local/bin/codex`? |
+|---|---|
+| Claude Code running locally on the Mac | Yes |
+| `codex-local` MCP through the desktop bridge | Yes, but the bridge returns an error after 60 s. Anything beyond a trivial ask times out on the caller's side even if Codex keeps working. |
+| Cowork / cloud session `device_bash` | **No.** That shell is an isolated Linux VM (`uname` reports Linux, `HOME=/sessions/...`) with only the connected folders mounted under `$HOME/mnt/`. `/Users` does not exist there. |
+| Cowork / cloud session `Bash` | No. Different machine entirely. |
+
+Verified 1 September 2026: `ls /Users` from `device_bash` returns
+`No such file or directory`, while `device_list_dir` on `~/Build/Digipomps`
+lists the real Mac paths. Reading Mac paths and executing on the Mac are
+different capabilities; only the first is available from a cloud session.
+
+A cloud or Cowork Claude therefore cannot start Codex itself, whatever the
+path. Its three options, in order:
+
+1. `codex-local` MCP, accepting the 60 s cap and the risk of an unobserved run
+2. computer use on the Mac, if it has been turned on
+3. a file handoff plus one line for Kjetil to paste:
+
+```bash
+/Users/kjetil/.local/bin/codex exec -C /Users/kjetil/Build/Digipomps/HAVEN \
+  "Les <handoff-fil> og utfør slicene som er merket godkjent."
+```
+
+Do not report that Codex is unavailable without naming which of these three was
+tried.
+
+
